  "generation_method": "Life stage -> career -> income -> household -> housing & debt -> spending -> savings & wealth -> risk -> behaviour -> goals, each step derived from the previous ones plus independent noise (see the generator docstring and README). Income: log-normal around education x city tier x experience curve x background, re-drawn (not clipped) outside 0.25 lakh-5 crore. Debt: annuity instalments at sampled rates/tenures/elapsed time. risk_label = ordinal thresholds (shares 13/42/33/12%) on 0.45*tolerance + 0.25*capacity + 0.15*horizon + 0.10*stability + 0.05*experience + N(0, 0.5). expense_segment drawn from prudence / lifestyle / leverage before the spending, debt and savings it shapes. behavior_anomaly = the 2.5% most impulsive active investors, each with one injected burst of 10-30 large buys. goal_feasibility from the production goal engine (core/goals.py) at 500 Monte Carlo paths per goal (the application uses 10,000); emergency-fund requirement from the production assess_emergency_fund.",
  "latent_variables": [
    "socio_economic_background",
    "prudence",
    "risk_tolerance",
    "leverage_propensity",
    "lifestyle",
    "stability",
    "investing_experience",
    "impulsivity"
  ],
  "target_side_columns": {
    "wealthpilot_customer_training.csv": [
      "risk_label",
      "expense_segment",
      "behavior_anomaly",
      "behavior_anomaly_month"
    ],
    "wealthpilot_goals_training.csv": [
      "monte_carlo_success_probability",
      "goal_feasibility",
      "inflation_adjusted_target_amount",
      "required_monthly_contribution",
      "contribution_gap",
      "goal_status"
    ]
  },
  "leakage_controls": [
    "Every target is generated from latent variables, never from an observed column; each observed feature carries independent noise.",
    "The validator requires that no single customer feature predicts risk_label with more than 70% accuracy (majority baseline 42%) and reports the strongest single features.",
    "Customer behaviour features use only transactions on or before feature_cutoff_date (re-computed and checked by the validator).",
    "Target-side columns and goal-engine outputs (inflation-adjusted target, required contribution, contribution gap, goal_status) must not be used as features.",
    "No train/test files are produced; split customers by customer_id (grouped) and transactions by date (time-ordered), never by random row shuffling."
  ],
  "goal_engine": {
    "module": "backend/wealthpilot/core/goals.py",
    "monte_carlo_simulations": 500,
    "application_monte_carlo_simulations": 10000,
    "return_periods_available": 74
  },
  "exports": {
    "far_trans_format": "customer_information, asset_information, transactions, close_prices in the FAR-Trans format (markets/limit_prices are not read by any loader and are not produced). investmentCapacity / customerType are assigned by wealth / standing rank to FAR-Trans's own shares; the EUR thresholds in the band names are not applied to INR amounts.",
    "kaggle_format": "synthetic_personal_finance_dataset.csv in the Kaggle personal-finance format.",
    "relationship": "All three shapes are views of ONE synthetic population. This is not a linkage of the real FAR-Trans and Kaggle datasets, which stay separate (ADR-010, ADR-039)."
  },
